{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And if from sixty years old and upward, etc.</b> When one reaches the days of old age, a woman is nearly equivalent to a man. Therefore a man, as he ages, declines by more than a third in his valuation, while a woman declines by only a third in her valuation. For people say: \"An old man in the house — a burden in the house; an old woman in the house — a treasure in the house and a good sign in the house\" (Arakhin 19)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:08:53.542773535Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}